WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.160
There are a lot of ways you can

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:03.290
establish status over another man,

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:05.660
like Jorge. A firm handshake.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.170
Displays of wealth.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.790
And feats of strength.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.450
*Groan* Interesting.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.080
Moving that rug was the hardest thing

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.280
in the world for you when I needed to

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.540
practice tap dancing.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.300
There are also more subtle moves, what I

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.100
call microaggressions.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.840
Call them by the wrong name.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.390
Throws them off the moment he meets

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.880
you. You must be Huevos!

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:30.680
Jay. Pleasure.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:31.790
Jorge De la Selva.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.320
In English, it's George of the jungle,

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.640
so I stick with Spanish.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.470
Hey, who's got the great taste?

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.340
That'd be me.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:38.600
Ha ha! Nice.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:44.060
Uh, hello. So you and Gloria used to.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.660
Yep. Ooh.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.090
Hey. So he was a little more handsome

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:51.290
than you were expecting, but pull

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.610
yourself together, man.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:56.210
So, Jorge, you were Gloria's boyfriend

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:57.710
right before Javier?

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.810
Yeah, And a little during, you know, she

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:01.130
kind of bounced around between the two

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:03.350
of us. Where is she, anyway?

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:04.550
I got to be at a Dodger game in an

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:05.210
hour.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.470
Oh, you like sports?

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.880
That's fantastic.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.810
I try to get this one into baseball.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:10.860
No-go.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.480
Actually, I hate baseball.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.490
I'm here to sing the national anthem.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.660
I'm an opera singer.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.520
I just finished two months at La Scala.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.530
The house that Toscanini built?

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:20.880
Yeah, well, it's been rebuilt a few

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.380
times. You know, a bunch of opera

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.430
singers prancing around.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.350
It takes its toll on the foundation.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:25.850
Yeah.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.660
Hey, I'm here to pick up Mom's old

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:28.860
boombox from storage.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.840
She needs it for...

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.270
How many nannies do you see through

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:33.870
these things?

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.850
That's Gloria's ex-boyfriend.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:37.380
Wait, how far ex?

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.850
Roughly 20 years.

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:41.510
Oh, my God. Is it possible?

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.350
What does Gloria say?

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.850
She hasn't even seen him yet.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.800
The odd bit is these two clones don't

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.480
see the resemblance. Maybe she won't

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.650
either. I'm not going to force it on

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.660
her. I mean, it's no easy thing to say.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.070
Is there a chance you're so dumb you

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.270
don't even know who the father of your

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:53.960
baby is?

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:55.250
We could do a DNA test.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.870
I could do one at the lab at school,

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.070
and then you would have a definitive

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.470
answer. If it comes back negative, you

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.850
don't even really have to tell Gloria.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.250
Well, what do you need? Saliva?

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.610
We take these two down to the Sizzler

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:05.900
and your squeegee, which you need off

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:06.890
the salad bar window.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.150
We use hairs now.

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:11.540
Good. You're home.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.120
One second. Papi, you look great in

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:15.350
that new shirt.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:16.910
So handsome.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:17.960
Hey Gloria.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.200
Oh, I thought you were Manny.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:22.520
Good. You're caught up now.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.860
I know I put on a few, but they don't

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:26.240
take you seriously as an opera singer

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:27.320
when you're too skinny.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.120
You know what happens when the thin

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.670
lady sings? The show just keeps going.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.800
It's so wonderful to see you.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.020
I'm going to go and open a bottle of

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:43.690
wine. Do you think that Jorge could be?

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.160
Jorge mentioned you bounced around

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.270
between him and Javier.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.130
How much bouncing did you do?

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.190
Technically, it's possible.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:52.900
Oh, my God.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.950
How is Manny going to handle this?

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.650
Not great! You know, he doesn't respond

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:57.990
well to surprises.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.950
Remember how upset he got when he found

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.240
out those mashed potatoes were really

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.410
just whipped cauliflower?

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:02.740
What are we

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:03.820
going to do?

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.920
Okay, Grandpa I got.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.480
.. Oh, Gloria, you're here.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:07.870
What do you

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.420
bring with you besides that guilty look?

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.640
Okay, In order to get a definitive

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.640
answer, I had Alex perform a DNA test.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.740
You got them both to spit?

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.300
They use hair now.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.270
Hey, lotion is on the sink, Jorge.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:23.590
Hey, Turns out I'm not the only one who

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:24.880
suffers from dry navel.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.930
Uh, Alex, why do you have a medical

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.130
form with my name on it?

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.110
I don't think I should be the one to

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:32.890
explain this.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.170
Manny, as you know, your mother and

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.940
Jorge had a relationship.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.400
You're a lot alike.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.390
And it made us curious as to whether

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.840
Uh, are you saying this is a DNA test?

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.670
Your mom didn't even find out until

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:51.420
today.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:56.100
Oh, I don't even know how to react.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.370
So my whole childhood was a lie.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.320
I thought Javier was my dad.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.030
Now he's just some stranger who gave me

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.410
baths. Listen, buddy.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.630
It's not who brings you into the world.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.190
It's what you do when you're there.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:09.840
You're not Javier.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.490
You're not this guy. You're you.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:13.170
And what you are is amazing.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.000
And for the record, I've been your dad

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.620
since you were ten. And I'm going to be

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.090
your dad until I'm gone.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.000
I love you. And I always will.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:22.950
I love you, too, Jay.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.060
Ha,ha ha.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.000
April Fools, huh?

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.760
Now, who doesn't understand a joke?

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.610
What? I never dated Jorge.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.430
He's the butcher at the grocery store.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.020
I just thought that he looked like

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:43.800
Manny.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:45.900
Why would you do that?

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.700
Because you said that I didn't

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.320
understand funny.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:50.820
I didn't know you were going to take the

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:53.130
prank this far. You made Grandpa cry.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.740
I know. He was like, "I love you.

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:58.730
And I Always will"

